WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.580 --> 00:04.710
When you find yourself in a less resilient mindset,
there's some good news.

2
00:05.290 --> 00:07.710
Research shows that mindsets are malleable.

3
00:08.330 --> 00:10.750
Not only can you change your mindset over time,

4
00:11.110 --> 00:13.250
you can even shift them in the short term.

5
00:14.150 --> 00:16.930
One way to have your mindset shifted is priming.

6
00:17.410 --> 00:25.760
For example, there are experiments in which students about to take an exam
were shown either intelligence words or neutral random words.

7
00:26.410 --> 00:32.070
You can guess that the students primed on intelligence
statistically achieved better results on their exam.

8
00:33.000 --> 00:39.390
This is why inspiring quotes, morning mantras, and other
self-priming techniques can be so effective.

9
00:40.130 --> 00:44.640
But there are times you need something more powerful
and pointed to shift your mindset.

10
00:45.190 --> 00:47.270
This is where the APR technique can help.

11
00:48.330 --> 00:54.500
The basic idea is that you bring awareness to your current mindset
and realize how it affects your behavior,

12
00:55.270 --> 00:58.850
pause to create a wedge in which you can
choose to do something differently,

13
00:59.330 --> 01:01.060
take on a different lens, so to speak,

14
01:01.890 --> 01:07.430
and use specific reflection questions to reframe
your mindset into one that serves you better.

15
01:08.290 --> 01:13.790
This in turn will help you respond through your behavior,
emotions and thoughts in a way you desire.

16
01:14.280 --> 01:16.510
This technique is very helpful in the moment.

17
01:17.190 --> 01:19.170
It's also helpful for the long term.

18
01:19.910 --> 01:28.930
The continual practice of APR can help change any entrenched mindsets
that have become the default from years of repetition and reinforcement.

19
01:30.250 --> 01:31.390
Now let's practice.
